From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] led: log supported short names at debug level

getLedDescr already supports one-part legacy labels and two-part
color:function names, with upstream coverage for both. Warning that they
are malformed contradicts the parser and produces warnings for the board's
bmc-heartbeat, fault and identify LEDs. Log supported short forms at debug
level, retaining warnings for unexpected part counts. Leave parsing, sysfs
names, D-Bus paths and physical LED control unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/sysfs.cpp
+++ b/sysfs.cpp
@@ -175,7 +175,15 @@
-    if (words.size() != 3)
+    if (words.size() == 1 || words.size() == 2)
+    {
+        // Legacy labels and shortened color:function names are supported
+        // by the parser below; they are not malformed LED descriptions.
+        lg2::debug(
+            "Using supported short LED description '{DESC}'",
+            "DESC", name);
+    }
+    else if (words.size() != 3)
     {
         lg2::warning(
             "LED description '{DESC}' not well formed, expected 3 parts but got {NPARTS}",
             "DESC", name, "NPARTS", words.size());
     }
 
